31,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems some roads close in winter, but community halls stay open. Also, the grants only cover session fees for a year.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The outer wards have lost bus links, making the trip an hour. Meanwhile, our rooms are full, but people use the catalogue late at night.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out! Outreach used to be super popular in outer wards, and some old evening groups are still going without any help!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The vehicle lines overran significantly last year. Also, the grant structure means we face a funding cliff after twelve months for operations.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We have retired tradespeople who can help with repairs, but no one on the payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, if the vehicle costs are so high and the grants are short, a mobile service might be very risky.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"But @Rin's discovery about the outer wards is crucial. People can't get to us, and they used to love the outreach.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,See! We should do something like those old groups that didn't need us to hold their hands.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,A mobile service is a financial trap if the running costs are volatile and the grant is temporary. We need something more stable.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,And we lack the supervisory staff for complex new facilitator-led programs. We should lean on existing community skills.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I worry that relying on external contractors for things like scanning might be just as unstable as the roads.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we can't move the library to the people, we must find a way to make the service accessible regardless of the bus.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,The old digitisation project failed because it wasn't indexed. We shouldn't just repeat that mistake!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. We need a model where the capital investment is handled by the endowment, not the fragile operating budget.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,The tool certification is also a problem; our expert retired. A workshop would need a new way to stay safe.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
