60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"We have four choices: a Mobile Branch, a Maker Workshop, Language Circles, or a Digital Archive.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Mobile Branch solves the bus issue, but @Benjamin mentioned the costs are unstable. Language Circles could work if they are partner-run.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,The Digital Archive sounds like the failed project from six years ago. I don't like it!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Maker Workshop uses the endowment for tools, which is stable. Language Circles rely on session fees that expire.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,The Workshop is risky because we have no certified technician. Language Circles need supervisors we don't have.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,The Mobile Branch is vulnerable to those winter road closures I found. It's not a reliable year-round promise.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If the Mobile Branch is out, Language Circles in community halls are the best way to reach the outer wards.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,But the old evening groups worked because they were independent! Language Circles fit that pattern.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"From a budget perspective, the Maker Workshop is the cleanest, but the staffing gap Minako mentioned is a logical hurdle.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"I agree. The Language Circles, if coordinated with partner organizations, shift the supervisory burden away from our staff.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel the Language Circles are the gentlest and most sustainable way to help our neighbors.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,They solve the accessibility problem without needing a bus or a van. I support them.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,They are like the successful old groups! I vote for the circles!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While the Workshop is financially attractive, the lack of a technician makes it impractical. Language Circles are a rational compromise.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Since they use partner organizations, it doesn't overload our current roster. I am convinced.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
